---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="What this site is about">
  <div class="container py-12">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">about</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose max-w-2xl">
      <p>
        This is where I document my experiments, side projects, and explorations.
        Think of it as a digital lab notebook - a place to track progress,
        share learnings, and keep myself accountable.
      </p>

      <p>
        Each experiment has its own page with a timeline of posts documenting
        the journey from idea to (hopefully) something interesting.
      </p>

      <h2>Why public?</h2>
      <p>
        Writing in public forces clarity. It's easy to convince yourself
        you understand something until you try to explain it. Plus, maybe
        someone else finds it useful.
      </p>

      <h2>The format</h2>
      <p>
        Each experiment starts with a question or goal. Posts document
        progress - what worked, what didn't, what I learned. Links to
        code, PRs, and resources where relevant.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you want to follow along, there's an <a href="/feed.xml">RSS feed</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
